      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-26T13:46:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It actually does work, but only if you don\u0027t do anything interesting with the type inline.  This usually means explicitly uninlining all constructors and the destructor.  E.g. sksg::Group is fwdeclared here: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/modules/skottie/src/text/TextAdapter.h;drc\u003da5c66fdd422c7fb01b446160e4f4af6d85e04d63;l\u003d23",
      "parentUuid": "f2772297_4767fcd4",
      "revId": "ed4e6716f0d9cee82755af00bc80919f5929b043",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87d5c22c_e5c93285",
        "filename": "modules/skottie/include/SlotManager.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T14:56:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The getters should be const.\n\nAlso, ideally getImageSlot should return a `const sk_sp\u003cSkImage\u003e\u0026`, so that we don\u0027t increment the refcount upfront - the client can decide whether to ref for ownership transfer (by converting to a non-const sk_sp\u003c\u003e) or use as const\u0026 for temp access.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "ed4e6716f0d9cee82755af00bc80919f5929b043",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
